ir Next', 'Avenir', sans-serif !important; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; min-height: 1em; margin: 0 0 12px; padding: 0;\"><em><strong>AUTHOR'S NOTE: </strong></em> Crypto doesn’t sleep or take holidays (neither will tradfi markets if recent proposals go through). <span> With ₿TC probing the LRR (low end of the Risk Range) and SOL/AVAX flirting with TREND shifts, we thought it worthwhile to pass through the updated Risk Ranges for today.  <br /></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"color: #252729; font-family: 'Karla', 'Proxima Nova', 'Avenir Next', 'Avenir', sans-serif !important; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; min-height: 1em; margin: 0 0 12px; padding: 0;\"><strong><span class=\"text-[#339EF3]\" style=\"color: #339ef3;\">holiday.rand(thoughts) …</span></strong> <span> </span>often times, rather than attempting to directly quantify the probability of something happening, it's easier to consider the probability of something not happening (and subtracting from 1).<span>  </span><span> </span>This can serve to (re)conceptualizes conditions in an intuitive way and helps psycho-emotionally recalibrate.<span>  </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"color: #252729; font-family: 'Karla', 'Proxima Nova', 'Avenir Next', 'Avenir', sans-serif !important; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; min-height: 1em; margin: 0 0 12px; padding: 0;\">In other words, if you find yourself having an emotional reaction to crypto price action, try a simple re-framing ... </p>\r\n<div>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: decimal; margin: 1em 0 1em 2.5em; padding: 0;\">\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: .5em; padding: 0;\">How realistic is it that markets will simply rise linearly with no chop and no drawdowns, always &amp; forever?</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: .5em; padding: 0;\">#1 .. but for speculative 80 vol assets!?</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: .5em; padding: 0;\">In the context of our process, the RiskRange = immediate-term weather for the day.<span>  </span>The TREND = the season (or the climate). 